# Enclave OS — apps the INSTALLED system gets, downloaded by the installer.
# Calamares installs these (pacman, from the Arch mirrors) right after it has
# copied the live system to the disk, so they never take space on the ISO.
# The live desktop still shows the pinned ones (Mail, Media Player): small
# preview stand-ins explain they come with the install, and are removed then.
# Format: one package per line; '#' comments. Needs an internet connection
# during install (the installer checks for one).

# --- Mail and media ---
thunderbird
celluloid
pavucontrol

# --- Fonts: every script (the live ISO only carries Inter, DejaVu, emoji) ---
noto-fonts
noto-fonts-cjk
ttf-liberation

# --- Linux apps from Flathub ---
flatpak

# --- Windows apps (Wine) and the 32-bit runtime it needs (multilib) ---
wine
winetricks
cabextract
lib32-mesa
lib32-vulkan-icd-loader
lib32-gnutls
lib32-pipewire
vulkan-tools

# --- Firmware for less common hardware (the live ISO keeps the common set) ---
linux-firmware-marvell

# --- Assistant / developer runtime (the assistant itself stays opt-in) ---
python-pip
python-pipx
python-virtualenv
python-keyring

# --- Manuals ---
man-db
man-pages
